# Terraform
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
crash.log
crash.*.log
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
tfplan
*.tfplan

# The bootstrap root module deliberately uses LOCAL state, because it creates the
# very S3 bucket that every other root module stores its state in. That state file
# is never committed. See README.md, "Bootstrapping the state backend", for why
# this is safe: the bootstrap is fully reproducible from code, and if the state
# file is lost the two resources can be re-imported in about a minute.
terraform/bootstrap/terraform.tfstate
terraform/bootstrap/terraform.tfstate.backup

# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored. The provider dependency
# lock file must be committed so every machine and every CI run resolves the exact
# same provider versions and checksums. Ignoring it is a common mistake.

# Real variable values and backend config. Only the .example files are committed.
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
*.auto.tfvars
backend.hcl

# Ansible
ansible/inventory/hosts.ini
*.retry
.vault_pass

# Tooling output
.checkov.baseline
results_*.json
report_*.json

# Local editor and OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
